Organizers record an increase in the number of bookings
It seems to be a good winter for German travel organizers:
According to one study, the sales volume of travel bookings over the next few months increased compared to last year - even the winter season by more than 30 per cent.
According to one study, in spite of the weakened conjuncture the desire to travel of the Germans remains as before.
Germany's (DVR) Journey Association (DVR) reported on Monday, with travel bookings for the Winter Preseason travel agencies recorded a sales volume that is 31 per cent higher compared to the same period last year.
According to research by market research institute GfK, bookings for the Autumn Stakes had already risen in numbers.
Thus the sales volume of travel agencies in October was almost eleven per cent higher compared to 2007, the DVR reported.
The basis of the results are GfK figures that are the information analyzed on bookings at 1,200 travel agencies and roughly computerized for the entire market.
The data collected are the travel bookings made until the end of August 2008.
Due to the weakened course of the dollar especially travels to the United States are in high demand, the DRV reported.
In this case the number of bookings increased by almost a third.
Germany's favourite points of destination are not only Spain, Turkey and Greece but also the regions of Germany.
Especially organized tours are very favorite, explains Klaus Laepple, the president of the DRV.
In view of the fact that energy and food prices increase, in this case travel costs are "better calculable for the customer than during an individual trip."
Among the other things, consumers can save money with pre-reserve discounts or All-Inclusive offers, Laepple explained.
Also in the summer's months, trips were well booked, so the volume of sales compared to last year rose again - although according to another study the number of Germans taking a trip, compared to last year, dropped.
